WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.950
We are going to look for the silence of zone C in relation to zone A on the

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.010
diaphragmatic plane.

3
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.760
There is a point of silence in the room.

4
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.850
At some point, I will guide you.

5
00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:15.560
We will start from neutral.

6
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.250
We will gradually allow the patient's neutral to develop.

7
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.240
We will focus on the micro-crystalline field.

8
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:26.500
We take up all the space.

9
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.090
The film on aikido.

10
00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:30.190
To have the most therapeutic action...

11
00:00:34.027 --> 00:00:37.707
as effective as possible, I must achieve a neutral state.

12
00:00:37.707 --> 00:00:42.417
Then, it is important to be able to bring out this neutral in my patient.

13
00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:45.067
It is something that must mature. And for

14
00:00:47.107 --> 00:00:48.907
that, we need the meeting point.

15
00:00:48.907 --> 00:00:51.897
Once I have a meeting point, the person, in confidence,

16
00:00:51.897 --> 00:00:54.237
can gradually disengage, let go towards their neutral.

17
00:00:54.237 --> 00:00:56.887
Gradually, these two neutrals will begin to blend.

18
00:00:56.887 --> 00:01:01.227
Once these two neutrals blend, I have a space, a more visible emergence that can

19
00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.647
appear from what we call primary respiration.

20
00:01:03.647 --> 00:01:06.307
Primary respiration is not something that is only in the body,

21
00:01:06.307 --> 00:01:09.647
it is present everywhere, a bit like the breath of life.

22
00:01:09.647 --> 00:01:10.781
We will just put ourselves

23
00:01:10.781 --> 00:01:13.149
in the awareness of this amniotic cavity, this

24
00:01:13.149 --> 00:01:17.479
zone B, and at the same time, little by little, we will dissociate our attention to

25
00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:19.241
go to the diaphragmatic pillars.

26
00:01:19.241 --> 00:01:22.482
These are the most fixed points of my diaphragm, they are pillars.

27
00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:25.952
And we will see that ultimately, these are enormous support points,

28
00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.152
almost a silent point.

29
00:01:27.152 --> 00:01:31.279
And we will gradually, with a little patience, bring out the neutral in a broader way.

30
00:01:31.279 --> 00:01:34.929
That is to say, we will also use the crystalline silence,

31
00:01:34.929 --> 00:01:38.799
we will rather speak of the crystalline immobility of the room.

32
00:01:38.923 --> 00:01:40.463
There is a kind of...

33
00:01:40.463 --> 00:01:44.483
In zone C, there is a kind of immobility that we must see.

34
00:01:47.323 --> 00:01:50.673
We will let the body center itself in relation to this zone C.

35
00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:56.375
Even if it seems subtle, it will happen by itself on a fluid, electrical plane.

36
00:01:56.375 --> 00:02:01.595
And then we will gradually, in this practice, begin to merge this silence of the

37
00:02:01.595 --> 00:02:06.055
room, or this dynamic immobility of the room, with the dynamic immobility at

38
00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:14.210
the level of the diaphragmatic pillars. While being aware...

39
00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:22.630
of the amniotic cavity and all the integration of my vitelline vesicle to form my

40
00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:23.260
venous system.

41
00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:27.470
In this practice, to totally surrender to primary respiration,

42
00:02:32.338 --> 00:02:35.898
to the present movement, to the tide, that is to say,

43
00:02:35.898 --> 00:02:41.168
to the therapeutic force, to the power, and gradually let's see what it can do.

44
00:02:41.168 --> 00:02:42.178
The "hueil", in

45
00:02:44.178 --> 00:02:47.938
non-action, meaning I don't induce, I trust.

46
00:02:48.406 --> 00:02:49.576
the osteopath

